      "quote": "we can always find a subset of the first $ i $ elements that sums to a value in $[190, 210]$.",
      "reason": "False: four 23s and five 24s total 212. Every proper subset sums to at most 189, while the whole list sums to 212. Thus N=10 is not sufficient."
    },
    {
      "quote": "there must be a **partial sum** that crosses from below 190 to above 210.",
      "reason": "A crossing that skips the target interval is not necessary. For ten 25s, partial sums include 200 between 175 and 225."
    },
    {
      "quote": "Let $ s_i $ be the first partial sum that exceeds 190. Then $ s_{i-1} < 190 $",
      "reason": "Only s_{i-1}≤190 follows. For nineteen 10s followed by 25, the preceding partial sum is exactly 190."
    }
  ],
  "unresolved_obligations": [
    "Determine the actual minimum N and prove its sufficiency for every permitted list; the submitted sufficiency claim is false."
  ],
